{"id": "EUVD-2026-94012", "enisaUuid": "23a9894f-2d06-3023-85cb-fcd15a18c11a", "description": "Backstage is an open framework for building developer portals. Prior to 0.16.1 and 0.17.8, the @backstage/backend-defaults package is affected by improper preservation of access restrictions during service credential delegation. An external service credential configured with access restrictions (e.g., read-only) could bypass those restrictions by routing requests through plugin delegation paths. This could allow a restricted service to perform operations beyond its intended scope, including write operations on plugins it was restricted to read-only access for. This issue is fixed in versions 0.16.1 and 0.17.8.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T20:48:05", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-09T01:51:07", "baseScore": 7.6, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:H/A:L", "references": ["https://github.com/backstage/backstage/security/advisories/GHSA-cq7v-rfgc-5c7v", "https://github.com/backstage/backstage/commit/40346245c53e1bf26dee56601e95c5c4ab9cc124", "https://github.com/backstage/backstage/commit/bc80ffdafbc92ff7b8c72347eace13cb8688fd33", "https://github.com/backstage/backstage/releases/tag/v1.49.6", "https://github.com/backstage/backstage/releases/tag/v1.54.6"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-106492", "GHSA-cq7v-rfgc-5c7v"], "assigner": "GitHub_M", "epss": 0.24, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0b4f51b1-9145-3bed-95a2-7d657c00a256", "product": {"name": "backend-defaults", "vendor": {"name": "@backstage"}}, "product_version": "< 0.16.1"}, {"id": "41f57b33-7cf0-38ed-9f37-1197c3ca969e", "product": {"name": "backstage", "vendor": {"name": "backstage"}}, "product_version": "1.50.0-next.0, < 1.54.6"}, {"id": "428eb363-cd18-34ba-9024-6238af48c11d", "product": {"name": "backstage", "vendor": {"name": "backstage"}}, "product_version": "< 1.49.6"}, {"id": "5150e5d7-4433-3bb4-b3ae-aa39b9c62d59", "product": {"name": "backend-defaults", "vendor": {"name": "@backstage"